<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, maximum-scale=1, user-scalable=no">
    <meta name="description" content="Terms for using the <%= business.name %> website and pet transport services.">
    <title>Terms of Service | <%= business.name %></title>
    <link rel="shortcut icon" type="image/png" href="/images/img/favicon.png">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com/" crossorigin>
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Poppins:wght@300;400;500;600;700;800&amp;display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
    <link href="/css/bootstrap.min.css" rel="stylesheet">
    <link href="/css/slicknav.min.css" rel="stylesheet">
    <link href="/css/all.min.css" rel="stylesheet">
    <link href="/css/custom.css" rel="stylesheet">
    <link href="/css/content-pages.css" rel="stylesheet">
<link href="/css/brand.css" rel="stylesheet">
<%- include('../partials/chat') %>
<link href="/css/zoom.css" rel="stylesheet">
</head>
<body>
    <%- include('../partials/site-header') %>
    <div class="page-header"><div class="container"><div class="page-header-box"><h2>Terms of Service</h2><nav aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol class="breadcrumb"><li><a href="index.html">Home</a></li><li>Terms of Service</li></ol></nav></div></div></div>

    <main class="content-page">
        <div class="container">
            <section class="content-intro">
                <div class="content-kicker">Service agreement</div>
                <h1>Terms for using our services</h1>
                <p>These terms describe the general conditions for using this website and requesting pet transport services from <%= business.name %>.</p>
            </section>

            <div class="legal-layout">
                <article class="legal-document">
                    <section class="legal-section"><h2>1. Acceptance of terms</h2><p>When you access this website, send an enquiry, accept a quote, or instruct us to start a service, you accept these terms along with the applicable written quote, booking confirmation, service-specific conditions, and mandatory carrier or authority requirements.</p></section>
                    <section class="legal-section"><h2>2. Our role</h2><p><%= business.name %> coordinates pet travel and may use independent drivers, airlines, veterinarians, handlers and other qualified partners. Your accepted quote or booking confirmation defines the scope of our responsibility.</p></section>
                    <section class="legal-section"><h2>3. Quotes and bookings</h2><p>Quotes reflect the information available when issued. They remain subject to capacity, route availability, airline acceptance, seasonal and breed restrictions, government fees, inspections, and your pet's final details. A booking is confirmed only after acceptance and written confirmation.</p><p>Changes to your pet's size or crate, the number of pets, the route, dates, pickup or delivery arrangements, or paperwork may affect pricing and schedules.</p></section>
                    <section class="legal-section"><h2>4. Customer responsibilities</h2><p>You are responsible for complete and accurate information about your pet, including breed, age, size, health and temperament, required veterinary documents and permits, correct contact details, and being available at pickup and delivery.</p></section>
                    <section class="legal-section"><h2>5. Restricted breeds and travel conditions</h2><p>Airlines and authorities may restrict some breeds, sizes, ages or travel in extreme weather. If a route is not safe or allowed for your pet, we will recommend an alternative, such as ground transport or a different travel date.</p></section>
                    <section class="legal-section"><h2>6. Government and entry requirements</h2><p>We guide you through destination requirements, but final decisions rest with airlines and government authorities. Unless agreed otherwise in writing, owners remain responsible for meeting entry rules and paying any official government fees directly to the government agency.</p></section>
                    <section class="legal-section"><h2>7. Collection, delivery, and timing</h2><p>Travel times and pickup or delivery windows are estimates unless a written service confirmation explicitly guarantees a deadline. Timing may be affected by weather, traffic, inspections, airline schedule changes, animal-welfare decisions, security events, owner availability, or other circumstances beyond reasonable control.</p></section>
                    <section class="legal-section"><h2>8. Pet transport</h2><p>Pet owners are responsible for veterinary advice, fitness-to-travel decisions, vaccinations, microchips, permits, approved crates, entry requirements, and accurate animal details. Carrier and authority approval is required for travel. Welfare or compliance concerns may lead us to recommend a different route or schedule.</p></section>
                    <section class="legal-section"><h2>9. Charges and payment</h2><p>Payment is due under the terms shown on the quote or invoice. Extra charges may only result from changes you request, inaccurate pet details, unsuccessful pickup or delivery, or services added after booking, and are always confirmed with you in writing first. We never ask for extra payment while your pet is travelling.</p></section>
                    <section class="legal-section"><h2>10. Loss, damage, and insurance</h2><p>Applicable law, airline terms and the agreed service scope may limit liability. Ask us about pet travel insurance before the journey, and tell us promptly about any concern at hand-over.</p></section>
                    <section class="legal-section"><h2>11. Cancellations and changes</h2><p>Changes or cancellations may incur charges once vehicle or airline space, travel crates, permits, or partner services have been reserved. Any refund depends on costs already incurred and the relevant carrier or provider’s conditions.</p></section>
                    <section class="legal-section"><h2>12. Website use</h2><p>Website material is general information and may change without notice. Misuse, unauthorized access, interference with the site, unlawful submissions, and reproduction of protected content without permission are not allowed.</p></section>
                    <section class="legal-section"><h2>13. Governing requirements and disputes</h2><p>The mandatory laws and transport conventions relevant to the contracting entity, route, service, and place of performance apply. Contact us first about concerns so we can review the booking records and supporting evidence and attempt a resolution.</p></section>
                    <section class="legal-section"><h2>14. Contact</h2><p>For questions about these terms or your booking, contact <a href="mailto:<%= business.email %>"><%= business.email %></a>.</p></section>
                </article>
                <aside class="legal-aside"><h2>Terms details</h2><p><strong>Effective date</strong><br>20 July 2026</p><p>Additional conditions for your service may appear in the accepted quote or booking confirmation.</p><p><a href="privacy-policy.html">Read our Privacy Policy</a></p></aside>
            </div>
        </div>
    </main>

    <%- include('../partials/site-footer') %>
    
    <script src="/js/jquery-3.7.1.min.js"></script>
    <script src="/js/bootstrap.min.js"></script>
    <script src="/js/jquery.slicknav.js"></script>
    <script src="/js/service-navigation.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
